        "comments": "The assembly csSphLind2.1 is based on 52x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Chromosome 22 is a microchromosome. Based on the PacBio read coverage it could be overcollapsed and exist in more than one copy. Chromosome 21 is about 1/4th of the size of an autosome, which is similar to what Healey, A.L., et. al (https://doi.org/10.1038/s41477-022-01333-5) observed for potential U/V sex chromosomes in other Sphagnums. Chromosome 20 seems to be made up of very repetitive sequence.",
